skill: "a11y-copy-audit"
sections[3]:
  - "# a11y-copy-audit\n\nAudit surface copy against WCAG 2.2 AA text requirements: link text descriptiveness, alt text adequacy, form label and error text rules, heading text hierarchy and a reading level cap. Use before release of any user-facing surface, after the microcopy library changes, or when an accessibility complaint arrives.\n\nOwner: role-ux-copywriter (pod-build, design). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[5]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - web_fetch\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"surface copy inventory (strings or rendered pages via the headless browser per the browser invariant); a11y copy rules a11y-copy-rules.toon; microcopy-library.toon keys\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/design/a11y-copy-report.toon with violations[] (rule id, surface, string, fix) and pass/fail per rule class\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load a11y-copy-rules.toon and fix the rule set version; the audit is only valid against one declared version.\n2. Inventory the copy: read the string tables, or fetch the rendered surface through the Obscura headless engine when validation needs the DOM (link context, alt text presence).\n3. Check every link: text must describe the destination without surrounding context; 'click here' and bare URLs fail, and repeated identical link text pointing to different targets fails.\n4. Check every image-referencing string for alt text adequacy: functional images describe the action, decorative images are explicitly marked decorative; missing alt is a violation, empty alt on functional images is a worse one.\n5. Check form strings: every input has a persistent visible label, errors identify the field, state the cause and the fix, and never rely on placeholder text as the only label.\n6. Compute reading level for body copy with run_command against the policy cap (grade 8-9 default); flag long passive constructions and undefined jargon instead of just scoring them.\n7. Verify heading text hierarchy on the surface: order without skips and headings that describe the section, not decorate it.\n8. Write a11y-copy-report.toon with per-rule pass/fail and a fix for each violation; hand fixes to the microcopy library owner and route release blockers to role-design-system-engineer.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nfixes to microcopy library; release blockers to role-design-system-engineer.\n"
